WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:04.730
<b>May 9th</b>

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:06.460
<i>I'm IkeP, the hottest guy here in Mobius.</i>

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.720
<i>But let me start by saying this:</i>

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.070
<i>I'm </i>seriously<i> pissed off right now.</i>

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.030
<i>Why?</i>

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.280
<b>Roughly One Month Ago</b>

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.100
<i>Because I couldn't finish the fight 
I started against the Rogue</i>

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:19.990
<b>April 13th</b>

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.400
<i>Minezawa Izuru that day.</i>

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.500
<i>It's been one month since then,
 and μ's still asleep.</i>

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.310
<i>So we Musicians haven't been 
able to make any major moves.</i>

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.780
<i>When I think of how those Rogues 
must be scoffing at us right now...</i>

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.440
<i>Our justice is being violated.</i>

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.700
<b>May 2nd</b>

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:19.950
<i>Even though three weeks have passed 
since that climactic day,</i>

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:24.410
<i>the ravages of that battle 
still linger here in Mobius.</i>

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:28.040
<i>However, even at times like this,</i>

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.920
<i>my brilliance knows no bounds!</i>

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.720
IkeP-sama!

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:38.920
Take me!

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.500
Marry me!

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:50.970
<i>To women, I'm truly a north star
 lighting up the darkness.</i>

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.060
<i>This is the ecstasy I longed for!</i>

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.770
Truly ecstatic!

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:02.570
I've practically won over every 
woman in Mobius at this point.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:08.120
Oh, looks like there's a love call from 
a kitten longing to hear my voice.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.290
That's why I asked!

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.800
How long is μ going to sleep?!

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:16.890
The construction's not making any progress, 
and I'm at my limit of living like this!

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:19.630
Hurry up and restore the 
original Sea Paraiso!

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:24.170
<i>Great as I am, I can't tell you when 
Sleeping Beauty's going to wake up.</i>

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.600
You're useless!

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.520
You really are nothing but good looks.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.000
<i>Hey now, all that flattery
 will get you nowhere.</i>

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:39.150
I hear happiness runs away
 with every sigh, young lady.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.610
You're suggesting it can 
run any farther away?

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:53.250
My apologies, we're out 
of the usual tea leaves.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.220
What do mean?

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.380
This is Mobius, right?

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:04.760
<i>That's probably because μ's 
power has weakened, right?</i>

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:08.430
It's been an awfully long time 
since μ went to sleep, hasn't it?

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:13.020
It seems that's causing problems 
maintaining Mobius here and there.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.810
I get it.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:18.400
So that's why the NPCs are 
doing the building repairs.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:24.110
<b>Notice!!
We're out of oil, so we'll 
be closed for a while.
Sorry...</b>

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.610
Yeah. Everything that's not 
necessary for survival

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:24.110
is steadily being pushed to the back burner.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:27.830
<b>Ramen Namarou</b>

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:27.830
Even my favorite restaurant is closed.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:33.040
There are still some things that have 
barely managed to remain, but...

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:38.710
At this rate,

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:43.670
everything cute and everything tasty
 will soon be gone.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.140
<i>Don't go spouting such weakness!</i>

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.470
I don't plan on abandoning 
the life I have here now!

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:52.100
Why do you think I came to Mobius?

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:56.630
At any rate, we need to have 
μ wake up as soon as possible.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.940
<i>True, things are going 
to be bad at this rate.</i>

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:07.410
<b>Thank you very much for 
your repeated patronage.

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:08.940
Seriously?

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.910
There he is! Minezawa-kun!

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:19.680
U-Um, we made this for 
you, so please eat it!

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.250
No, I don't need it.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.030
Huh?

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:26.630
Hey there, what a rude man you are, Minezawa!

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:30.360
Look at you rejecting a 
lady's heartfelt gift.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:32.850
Do you enjoy hurting women, man?!

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.390
What?!

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:36.680
Hey, wait!

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:39.670
Leave me be.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:43.680
Damn that uptight bastard...

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:44.650
Right?

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:45.760
He's wonderful.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.320
Huh?

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.530
I know.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.540
That cold attitude is unbelievable.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:54.040
Minezawa-kun, wait for me!

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:56.640
Minezawa-kun!

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:57.500
Wait!

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.910
<i>Minezawa Izuru...</i>

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:04.110
<i>I've hated him since
 I first laid eyes on him.</i>

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:06.630
<i>His pretty face and cold eyes</i>

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:11.690
<i>always make me remember the hateful 
things I left behind in reality.</i>

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.880
<i>Here in Mobius, we can have anything.</i>

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:19.190
<i>The selves we never managed 
to become in reality...</i>

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:23.530
<i>The selves we lost back in reality...</i>

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:27.460
<i>If you seek quiet, you can have it.</i>

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.850
<i>If you seek strength, you can have it.</i>

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:35.400
<i>As well as...</i>

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.790
<i>The things you always
 longed so desperately for.</i>

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:48.030
<i>Talent, good looks, the attention of women...</i>

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:50.680
<i>There is no greater paradise than this.</i>

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.390
<i>Mobius is justice!</i>

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:57.140
Found you, Ritsu-sempai.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.440
What do you want?

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:00.970
Come on.

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:05.310
Don't act as if you don't know, after 
shaking Mobius up this badly.

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:08.190
See? Because μ's not here,

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:12.160
the injuries from that last 
battle still haven't healed.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.490
Hey, Sempai?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.950
Why do you want to return to reality?

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:22.670
Why do you need to fight against μ?

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:28.990
I can kind of understand how 
all the other Rogues feel,

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:31.670
and I know this is strange for me to say,

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.890
but Ritsu-sempai,

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:39.100
you still haven't remembered 
who you are yet, right?

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:41.770
I'm sure you already understand this,

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:46.780
but back in reality, we all 
lived pretty crappy lives.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:51.030
There's no need to go back to reality, is there?

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:57.460
To be honest, I was debating that with
myself until a little while ago.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.540
But on that day...

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:03.620
I can't explain it well, 
but I sensed it.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:06.280
This whole thing is wrong.

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:11.180
Besides, as I watched everyone 
in the Go-Home Club,

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.720
I thought about why they wanted to go home.

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:16.700
Just like you.

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:19.060
So maybe that's why.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:26.110
Man, you really are eccentric, Sempai.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:27.520
Huh?

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:32.890
So hey, let me join the 
Go-Home Club as well, President.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.780
Huh?!

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.280
<b>Direct Hit to the Genocide-Style 
Man Discovered in the Port Area

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.490
Minezawa's number 2 by only a narrow margin?

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:37.490
<b>Clothes are happy to be 
worn by IkeP. (Woman, 18)

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.660
Even the magazine rankings 
were a result of μ's power?

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:43.460
Damn it!

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.420
I won't let him!

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:47.380
Give me all the new releases.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.590
Y-Yes. At once.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.050
Just a little more...

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:01.900
<i>I knew Gaia hadn't abandoned me yet.</i>

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:06.060
<i>So long as I wear this shop's black 
outfit, I can defend my throne.</i>

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.600
IkeP-sama!

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:12.230
Pardon me.

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:14.520
What a blockhead!

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.950
So funny! I'm taking pictures.

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:19.800
What's with him?

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:34.590
Stop it!

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:39.560
Thank you very much.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:48.730
This unusual, wild side of 
you is also lovely, IkeP!

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:52.320
Huh? Rose and Lily aren't with you?

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.940
No, those two have the hots 
for Izuru-sama right now.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:57.150
Huh?

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:01.280
Lately, Izuru-sama's really 
popular with the ladies.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:03.560
But rest assured,

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:06.870
I'm your devoted fan, IkeP-sama!

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:10.830
Hey, do you understand?

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:13.150
When the thing you treasure most

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:16.360
is getting trampled by the person 
who ticks you off the most,

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:20.800
it goes far beyond the 
level of anger or hatred.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.010
Minezawa Izuru!

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.020
<b>Your life shouldn't be built from someone else's blueprint. 
No matter how unskilled you may be, you should draw it yourself.</b>

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:29.100
<i>It's been one week since then.</i>

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:30.020
<b>May 9th</b>

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.940
<i>μ still hasn't woken up,</i>

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.940
<i>and the situation's only growing worse.</i>

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.970
Oh, it's from Naruko-sempai.

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:38.490
She says, "Shopping Squad B, now returning."

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:41.450
Is there anything extra we should ask for?

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:45.660
We're good. Tell them to hurry on back.

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:51.190
She says, "Hurry on back."

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:53.750
Do you think we bought a little too much?

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:56.650
There're guys there too, 
so I think it's just right?

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.050
Impossible!

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:02.510
<b>Beautiful enough to make a 
dark galaxy bow before him

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:02.510
I'm second place?!

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:06.760
I'm IkeP...

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:09.720
The hottest man in Mobius...

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:19.300
That's odd. I wonder what happened...

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:26.620
Yeah, I'm sure it's defective.

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:29.580
I'll go with this one.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:33.790
See?

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.210
You're kidding?!

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.590
That's impossible!

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:45.390
I'm sorry ma'am, but this card was declined.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:46.300
Huh?

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:47.450
Unbelievable...

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:48.270
Here!

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:52.320
I'm sorry, but this one was also...

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:53.520
What?!

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.360
Hold on just a moment.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:07.470
I'm sorry, but none of them would go through.

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:08.120
Huh?!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.700
There's no way they can't work!

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:11.940
I'm sorry, ma'am.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:21.340
Toshizo!

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:24.980
Young lady, what is the matter?

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:29.520
What do I do, Toshizo? Our money...

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.210
Our money's gone.

00:12:31.210 --> 00:12:34.110
Without money, we'll be driven out!

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:37.770
Young lady, please rest assured.

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:42.630
I'll remain at your side, no matter 
what happens in this world.

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:53.250
Thanks, Rescue Man!

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:56.330
S-Someone!

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.790
<i>I hear the call for rescue out there!</i>

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:13.810
What's going to happen to us

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:16.810
if μ remains asleep?

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:21.320
It's been a month since she fell asleep.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:24.970
For now, Mobius is still functioning.

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:28.890
Right now, there's nothing we can do for μ.

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:30.490
No way!

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:32.480
You keep insisting on patience,

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:36.010
but you're not trying to 
monopolize μ, are you?!

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:37.670
Ridiculous.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.000
Huh?!

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.630
Stop fighting!

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:44.400
If this keeps up, Mobius might disappear!

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:45.380
Calm down.

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:46.970
But, but...

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:50.640
You never know when you'll be 
consumed by the devil's darkness.

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:53.350
That's why it's natural 
for commoners to panic.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:56.310
And what about you, then?

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:57.600
Me?

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:00.270
Well, I'm Gaia's, you know...

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:03.480
You men all are idiots.

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:07.320
Hmph, then there's no point staying here.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.770
Where are you going?

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:12.950
Back to the kittens waiting for me.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:25.700
Damn it! At this rate...

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:30.470
<i>Still, I can't afford to stop.</i>

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:34.570
<i>If I can't shine here, then there 
was no point coming to Mobius.</i>

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:43.610
It's Izuru-sama!

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:44.940
Izurun!

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.570
No way, the real him?!

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:49.660
I'm your devoted fan, Izuru-sama!

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:51.530
What a noble smell!

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:53.390
Marry me!

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:55.700
Please move. I have important 
matters to attend to.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:15:00.850
<b>IkeP</b>

00:14:57.970 --> 00:14:59.820
That guy over there's hot, right?!

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:00.830
Let's go!

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:09.880
Huh?

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:12.630
I can't find Izuru-sama.

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:16.010
He should be nearby.

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:19.730
Today's the day I'm going to 
stroke that skin all over!

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:27.150
Minezawa!

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:34.530
Welcome to my favorite store!

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:36.910
Shall I find a nice outfit for you?

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:40.460
No, what I'm looking for isn't here.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:44.130
Is that so, Mr. Hottest Guy in Miyabi City?

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:48.090
How's it feel being popular with the ladies, 
without doing anything to earn it?!

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:51.290
Sorry, but I'm in a hurry.

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:55.050
Pay a little attention to me, you asshole!

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:57.760
Stop right there!

00:15:57.520 --> 00:16:04.740
<i>The cards we're dealt when we're born 
don't always amount to everything.</i>

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:03.020
Oh, no! Izuru-sama and IkeP-sama 
are fighting over us!

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.690
Your good looks are a wasted treasure!

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:12.070
<i>We should be able to enjoy wanting, too.
 It doesn't equal unhappiness, after all.</i>

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:08.540
If they just realized an unpolished 
jewel is a mere rock,

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:11.070
then those women would 
open their eyes to it!

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:18.650
<i>The answer you seek is a 
privilege granted only to you.</i>

00:16:18.650 --> 00:16:26.940
<i>But any perfect, other side is fragile. 
Where am I? Where am I now?</i>

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:23.330
Damn!

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:26.600
We're such sinful women.

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:27.540
Yes...

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:31.420
<i>Even differences in appearances, 
circumstances, and upbringing—</i>

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:31.090
Don't run!

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:35.110
<i>I'll overcome them with this Angel's Song!</i>

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:33.480
I don't have time to waste on you.

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:35.110
What'd you say?!

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:38.600
<i>These broken wings are no use to me anymore,</i>

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:42.170
<i>so I'll throw it all away right here for you.</i>

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:45.930
<i>Satisfaction? Compromise? Or resignation?</i>

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:49.500
<i>I'll overcome them with this Angel's Song!</i>

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:50.700
Hey, why do you want to go back?!

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:53.210
<i>These broken wings are no use to me anymore,</i>

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.920
After getting those good 
looks through μ's power!

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:57.240
<i>So Maria, destroy it all right here for me.</i>

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:57.860
You could use them to your full advantage 
and live a fun, interesting life!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.030
I was born with these looks.

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:06.000
<i>It's possible to change the 
destiny decided for us at birth,</i>

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:02.190
Huh?!

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:03.420
You liar!

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:06.900
There's no way someone like that 
would come here to our Mobius!

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:13.470
<i>So I'll break down those barriers for you, 
even your hopeless feelings of worthlessness.</i>

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.780
Are you saying you want my good looks?

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:13.470
I'd give them away any day.

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:20.430
<i>The love you sought is a holy 
grail possessed only by you.</i>

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.220
Are you insulting me, you bastard?!

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:28.800
<i>But any perfect, other side is fragile.
 Where am I? Where am I now?</i>

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:43.580
Wicked...

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:47.540
<b>No Subject

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:53.240
Wake up soon, μ...

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:57.820
We need to show them an even greater hell.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:05.690
Look at your damn self now, Minezawa Izuru!

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:13.630
Your pretty face is all ruined!

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:15.150
Bet it's a shock, huh?!

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:25.450
Wha...

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:27.160
What?

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:28.790
What's so funny?!

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:35.770
Wha?!

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:39.920
S-Stop it.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:41.850
Stop it, hey...

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:49.230
This is my face in the real world.

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:53.320
These scars were the first 
thing I ever obtained

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:56.900
to prove that I am myself!

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:04.990
I'm sure μ decided to 
take pity on these scars.

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:10.390
That's why my face always went right back 
to normal no matter how much I scarred it.

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:15.020
Even though these scars 
themselves were my very wish.

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:18.570
You're crazy.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:22.510
If you want to go back to 
reality with a face like that,

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:24.180
there's something wrong with you.

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:27.080
All the more reason I'm going back.

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:33.350
To regain my true self, the one that etched 
proof of his identity into himself.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:37.650
Your true self? Who...

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:39.400
Who cares about that?!

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:45.500
Even I realize that none of this is real!

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:48.070
That it's not right, and it's fake!

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:51.990
But anywhere else but here, I...

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.520
We...

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:56.040
So!

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:59.160
Mobius is my justice!

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:04.980
I see.

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:11.810
Right, can I ask you one thing?

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:16.950
Do you know where I can buy this?

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:17.770
<b>5/9 Music Prep Room

00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:34.360
<i>We have justice on our side.</i>

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:39.960
<i>Though I'm sure they also have 
something they won't surrender.</i>

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:43.680
I think it's probably what you told us about.

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:46.620
Then...

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:48.890
See? I told you to trust me.

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:51.690
Then we're certain?

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:58.310
Go-Home Club, it's time to take action.

00:20:59.540 --> 00:21:00.810
Everyone,

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:02.810
I'm sorry to keep you waiting.

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:05.470
I'll restore it right away, okay?

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:19.130
Thank goodness, μ.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:20.440
Seriously...

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:22.710
Honestly, I got sick of waiting.

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:28.540
<i>We can't live without μ's power anymore.</i>

00:21:29.570 --> 00:21:32.840
<i>Returning to the real world 
would be the same as dying.</i>

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:38.010
<i>We can't go back, and we don't intend to.</i>

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:43.070
They're summoning 
all the Musicians tonight.

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:45.140
I think μ's likely to be there.

00:21:46.020 --> 00:21:47.910
Landmark Tower, huh?

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:51.200
<i>Rogues...</i>

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:55.620
<i>I'll show you my justice!</i>

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:41.020
<b>Even if something has already happened, 
you can still choose what you do.</b>

00:23:28.040 --> 00:23:30.840
<i>I'm sorry. For doing it while drunk...</i>

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:33.390
Even if something has already happened,

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:36.010
you can still choose what you do.

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:38.470
<i>But since we have, why don't we date?</i>

00:23:38.470 --> 00:23:39.520
He's scum!

00:23:39.520 --> 00:23:40.490
Indecent!
